00:00:35.249 --> 00:00:41.680
The role of a manager is evolving.&nbsp;We’re moving away from that micromanaging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.560
where managers are expected to hold your&nbsp;
hand, and are constantly checking up on you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.360
or looking over your shoulder to make sure that&nbsp;
you’re doing what you’re supposed to be.&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:59.120
Instead of being spoon-fed, managers are now&nbsp;
focussing on clearly communicating goals,&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:06.240
facilitating teamwork and collaboration while also, encouraging a more independent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.720
working style. Let’s stop right there&nbsp;
and do a quick breakdown of the language.&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:21.280
Today we’re looking at conjunctions.
Conjunctions are used to add two sentences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.640
or two parts of a sentence together.
You would know things like “and” or “but”.&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.720
Today, we are using “while”.
We used it like this:&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:38.960
Managers are clearly communicating goals while&nbsp;
also encouraging a more independent work style.&nbsp;

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.640
Here, while has the meaning of 'at the same&nbsp;
time'. It’s important to note, in the UK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.160
we typically use “while”, and in the US,&nbsp;
“whilst” is a little bit more common.&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.360
The choice is up to you, both&nbsp;
are OK, you can use either.&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.840
Having an agile management&nbsp;
style means that managers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:06.320
are better able to support the different&nbsp;
and changing roles of their team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.571
helping them find the most suitable way, and&nbsp;
the most effective way to get the job done.&nbsp;

